# --- Data -------------------------------------------------------------------
# See the data/ rule in CLAUDE.md. Short version: processed aggregates are small
# and travel with the repo; raw day-files and anything bulk never do.

# Raw day-file cache and download manifests. This is where bulk accumulates.
data/raw/

# Parquet is binary, so git stores a FULL COPY on every change rather than a
# diff. Ignore it everywhere by default...
*.parquet

# ...except the processed aggregates, which are ~115 KB in total and let a
# teammate start on M2/M3 without a 40 MB pull. Keep an eye on the size: if
# these grow past ~1 MB, drop the exemption rather than letting history swell.
!data/processed/*.parquet

# ...but NEVER the injected ones. Synthetic generation data does not belong in a
# publicly judged repo sitting beside the real measurements — a reader cannot
# tell them apart from the filename alone, and that is exactly the confusion the
# BUILT/SIMULATED discipline exists to prevent. Regenerate with a seed instead:
#   python pipeline/fault_injection.py --ladder --seed 42
data/processed/*_injected.parquet
pipeline/output/ground_truth.json
pipeline/output/dispatch_injected.json

# The PVGIS Klang pull is a small reference artifact for the pitch, tracked
# deliberately.
!data/pvgis-bukit-raja-klang.json

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/web/.gitignore covers the frontend in detail; these catch strays
# anywhere else in the tree.
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
.vite/

# --- Environment ------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example IS committed — it documents which variables exist without
# leaking any values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
tmp/
scratch/

# Stray root lockfile. The only npm project is apps/web; an empty lockfile at
# the root confuses monorepo build detection and belongs to nothing.
/package-lock.json

# --- Claude Code (personal, not project) -------------------------------------
# Personal skill packs mirrored in here from the user's own machine so Claude
# has them available in this repo — not SolaraX-authored, not something a
# teammate cloning the repo needs, and ~9 MB is a lot to carry in git history
# for someone else's tooling. Reinstall locally rather than committing it.
.claude/skills/
# Local permission/hook overrides are machine-specific by convention; a
# project-shared .claude/settings.json (if one is ever added) still gets
# tracked normally.
.claude/settings.local.json
